." mdview manual page for Linux
.TH MDVIEW 1 "2026-04-02" "mdview 0.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
mdview \- render Markdown or plain text with an internal viewer
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B mdview
.RI [ \-h ]
.RI [ \-\-verify\-resize\-detection ]
.RI [ \-\-test\-input\-feedback ]
.RI [ \-\-reflow ]
.RI [ \-\-reflow\-mode
.I MODE
.RI ]
.RI [ \-\-noreflow ]
.RI [ \-\-verbose ]
.RI [ \-\-stdin\-timeout\-in\-seconds
.I SECONDS
.RI ]
.RI [ \-\-max\-stdin\-buffer\-megabytes
.I MEGABYTES
.RI ]
.RI [ \-\-MIL ]
.RI [ \-\-readability\-first\-tables ]
.RI [ \-\-no\-table\-borders ]
.RI [ \-\-no\-cell\-borders ]
.RI [ \-\-automation\-timeout
.I SECONDS
.RI ]
.RI [ \-\-automation\-timeout\-screenshot
.I BASENAME
.RI ]
.RI [ \-\-screen\-dump\-dir
.I DIRECTORY
.RI ]
.RI [ \-\-viewport\-columns
.I COLUMNS
.RI ]
.RI [ \-\-viewport\-rows
.I ROWS
.RI ]
.RI [ \-\-automation\-json
.I SOURCE
.RI ]
.RI [ \-\-redraw\-check\-digit ]
.RI [ \-V ]
.RI [ path " ..." ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
mdview renders Markdown and plain text with ANSI styling and displays content
through its internal viewing engine. When no document paths are supplied,
non-interactive stdin is treated as a buffered pipe-target candidate. When the
buffered document has clear valid Markdown structure, mdview renders it as
Markdown. Otherwise it falls back to plain-text rendering so arbitrary process
output is not reformatted accidentally.
.PP
For pure text files, default behavior preserves source line breaks and does
not reflow unless reflow is explicitly enabled. Markdown reflows to viewport
width by default. Markdown tables may exceed viewport width when minimum table
sizing requires overflow. Recognized pipe tables render as gray boxed grids by
default.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B path
Path to a Markdown or text file to view. When no paths are supplied, mdview
may buffer a non-interactive stdin document instead. Buffered stdin uses a
16 MB safety ceiling by default and stops waiting after 2 seconds of idle time
once bytes have started arriving. If no bytes arrive before that timeout,
stdin is treated as absent and mdview reports the normal missing-input error.
.TP
.BR \-h , " \-\-help"
Show the help message and exit.
.TP
.BR \-\-verify\-resize\-detection
Run the interactive resize-detection checklist and report PASS or FAIL.
.TP
.BR \-\-test\-input\-feedback
Run a two-stage terminal input diagnostic. Stage 1 uses direct terminal input
and line-oriented redraws. Stage 2 uses the full-screen
.BR prompt_toolkit
viewer stack. Both stages accept Left/Right arrows plus
.B ,
and
.B .
alternates and emit timestamped debug logs to standard error.
.TP
.BR \-\-reflow
Enable reflow processing. If no explicit mode is supplied, prose mode is used.
.TP
.BR \-\-reflow\-mode " " MODE
Select reflow policy mode:
.IR prose ,
.IR all ,
or
.IR none .
.TP
.BR \-\-noreflow
Disable reflow in all cases (equivalent to mode none).
.TP
.BR \-\-verbose
Report key operational events, including document switches in multi-document
sessions.
.TP
.BR \-\-stdin\-timeout\-in\-seconds " " SECONDS
Stop waiting for additional stdin bytes after SECONDS have elapsed with no
further input.
.TP
.BR \-\-max\-stdin\-buffer\-megabytes " " MEGABYTES
Refuse buffered stdin documents larger than MEGABYTES unless the operator
explicitly raises the safety ceiling.
.TP
.BR \-\-MIL , " \-\-mil"
Enable Monkey-in-the-Loop telemetry: emit operator action events and targeted
troubleshooting context.
.TP
.BR \-\-readability\-first\-tables
Always use readability-first table layout, even when fit-first could fit the
viewport.
.TP
.BR \-\-no\-table\-borders
Suppress outer Markdown table borders and leave whitespace gaps at the table
edges.
.TP
.BR \-\-no\-cell\-borders
Suppress internal Markdown table cell borders and leave whitespace gaps
between cells.
.TP
.BR \-\-automation\-timeout " " SECONDS
Inject synthetic quit after the given viewer runtime for automation runs.
.TP
.BR \-\-automation\-timeout\-screenshot " " BASENAME
Write timeout-exit framebuffer artifacts using BASENAME, producing
.B BASENAME.txt
and
.B BASENAME.attrs.json.
If omitted while automation timeout is enabled, mdview uses default basename
.B mdview-automation-timeout-framebuffer
in the current working directory.
.TP
.BR \-\-screen\-dump\-dir " " DIRECTORY
Choose the directory used when the interactive pager writes manual
.B !
captures as
.B mdview-screen.txt
and
.B mdview-screen.attrs.json.
The default is the current working directory.
.TP
.BR \-\-viewport\-columns " " COLUMNS
Override detected viewport width with a synthetic value.
.TP
.BR \-\-viewport\-rows " " ROWS
Override detected viewport height with a synthetic value.
.TP
.BR \-\-automation\-json " " SOURCE
Replay key events from JSON SOURCE. SOURCE may be a file path or literal JSON
string encoded as:
.B [[delay_seconds, key_spec], ...]
where delays are non-negative and key specs describe replayed key input.
.TP
.BR \-\-redraw\-check\-digit
Overlay a center-screen digit that advances from 0 to 9 on each interactive
pager redraw.
.TP
.BR \-V , " \-\-version"
Show the mdview version and exit.
.SH FILES
.TP
.B posix/mdview-help.txt
The shared POSIX help text derived from the argparse configuration. Keep this
file in sync with the parser when packaging the Linux man page.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR prompt_toolkit (7),
.BR curses (3x),
.BR terminfo (5)
